Here's a simple SystemVerilog module for an LDPC (Low-Density Parity-Check) encoder for FPGA implementation:

```verilog
module ldpc_encoder(
    input wire clk,
    input wire reset,
    input wire data_in,
    output wire data_out,
    parameter integer PARITY_CHECK_SIZE = 8
);

reg [PARITY_CHECK_SIZE - 1:0] parity_check;

always @(posedge clk or posedge reset)
begin
    if (reset)
    begin
        parity_check <= 0;
    end else
    begin
        // Implementation of LDPC encoding algorithm goes here
        // ...
    end
end

assign data_out = parity_check;

endmodule
```

This module has a clock input (clk), a reset input (reset), and an input data signal (data_in). It also has an output data signal (data_out) and a parameter for the size of the parity check (PARITY_CHECK_SIZE). The module implements the LDPC encoding algorithm in the always block, which is triggered by the positive edge of the clock or the positive edge of the reset signal. The encoded data is then assigned to the output data signal (data_out).

Note that this is a simplified example and the actual implementation of the LDPC encoding algorithm will depend on the specific requirements and constraints of your FPGA design.

