Here's a simple JavaScript function that switches the order of adjectives in a sentence:
```javascript
function switchAdjectives(sentence) {
  const words = sentence.split(' ');
  const adjectives = words.filter(word => word.match(/^[a-zA-Z]+$/)); // Filter out non-alphabetical words
  const reversedAdjectives = adjectives.reverse();

  const newSentence = words.map((word, index) => {
    if (adjectives.includes(word)) {
      return reversedAdjectives[index];
    } else {
      return word;
    }
  }).join(' ');

  return newSentence;
}

const originalSentence = "Beautiful green trees are in the park";
const newSentence = switchAdjectives(originalSentence);
console.log(newSentence); // Output: "Green beautiful trees are in the park"
```
This function first splits the sentence into an array of words. It then filters out non-alphabetical words and reverses the order of the adjectives. Finally, it maps through the original sentence array and replaces each adjective with its corresponding reversed adjective. The resulting sentence is returned.

