To fix the CORS error in WordPress when using Next.js, you can follow these steps:

1. Install the `cors` package in your Next.js project:
```bash
npm install cors
```
or
```bash
yarn add cors
```
2. Create a new file named `cors.js` in your `pages/api` directory.
3. Add the following code to the `cors.js` file:
```javascript
import { Cors } from 'cors';

const cors = new Cors({
  methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'DELETE'],
  allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'],
  origin: 'https://your-wordpress-site.com' // Replace with the domain of your WordPress site
});

export default async (req, res) => {
  await cors.handleRequest(req, res);
};
```
Replace `https://your-wordpress-site.com` with the domain of your WordPress site.
4. In your Next.js app, import the `cors.js` file and use it as a middleware function:
```javascript
import express from 'express';
import cors from '../../pages/api/cors';

const app = express();

app.use(cors);

// Your other routes go here

export default app;
```
5. Save your changes and restart your Next.js development server.

Now, when you make requests from your Next.js app to your WordPress site, the CORS error should be resolved.

